ce":"விடுதி","parts":[{"text":"விடு","lemma":"விடு","gloss":"give"},{"text":"தி","lemma":"தி","gloss":"you"}],"gloss":"you give"},{"surface":"ஆயின்","parts":[{"text":"ஆயின்","lemma":"ஆயின்","gloss":"if"}],"gloss":"if"},{"surface":"சிறிது","parts":[{"text":"சிறிது","lemma":"சிறிது","gloss":"small"}],"gloss":"small"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"குன்றியும்","parts":[{"text":"குன்றி","lemma":"குன்றி","gloss":"kunri seed"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"even"}],"gloss":"even a kunri seed"},{"surface":"கொள்வல்","parts":[{"text":"கொள்","lemma":"கொள்","gloss":"accept"},{"text":"வல்","lemma":"வல்","gloss":"I will"}],"gloss":"I will accept"},{"surface":"கூர்","parts":[{"text":"கூர்","lemma":"கூர்","gloss":"sharp"}],"gloss":"sharp"},{"surface":"வேல்","parts":[{"text":"வேல்","lemma":"வேல்","gloss":"spear"}],"gloss":"spear"},{"surface":"குமண","parts":[{"text":"குமண","lemma":"குமண","gloss":"O Kumanan!"}],"gloss":"O Kumanan!","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அதற்பட","parts":[{"text":"அதற்பட","lemma":"அதற்பட","gloss":"in the proper way"}],"gloss":"in the proper way","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"அருளல்","parts":[{"text":"அருள்","lemma":"அருள்","gloss":"bestow grace"},{"text":"அல்","lemma":"அல்","gloss":"verbal noun suffix"}],"gloss":"bestowing grace"},{"surface":"வேண்டுவல்","parts":[{"text":"வேண்டு","lemma":"வேண்டு","gloss":"request"},{"text":"வல்","lemma":"வல்","gloss":"I do"}],"gloss":"I request"},{"surface":"விறல்","parts":[{"text":"விறல்","lemma":"விறல்","gloss":"victory"}],"gloss":"victorious"},{"surface":"புகழ்","parts":[{"text":"புகழ்","lemma":"புகழ்","gloss":"fame"}],"gloss":"fame"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"வசையில்","parts":[{"text":"வசை","lemma":"வசை","gloss":"blemish"},{"text":"இல்","lemma":"இல்","gloss":"without"}],"gloss":"faultless"},{"surface":"விழு","parts":[{"text":"விழு","lemma":"விழு","gloss":"noble"}],"gloss":"noble"},{"surface":"திணை","parts":[{"text":"திணை","lemma":"திணை","gloss":"lineage"}],"gloss":"lineage"},{"surface":"பிறந்த","parts":[{"text":"பிற","lemma":"பிற","gloss":"be born"},{"text":"ந்த","lemma":"ந்த","gloss":"past participle suffix"}],"gloss":"born in"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"இசை","parts":[{"text":"இசை","lemma":"இசை","gloss":"fame"}],"gloss":"fame"},{"surface":"மேந்தோன்றல்","parts":[{"text":"மேந்தோன்றல்","lemma":"மேந்தோன்றல்","gloss":"eminent lord"}],"gloss":"eminent lord","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"நின்","parts":[{"text":"நின்","lemma":"நின்","gloss":"you"}],"gloss":"you"},{"surface":"பாடிய","parts":[{"text":"பாடு","lemma":"பாடு","gloss":"sing"},{"text":"இய","lemma":"இய","gloss":"past participle suffix"}],"gloss":"who sang"},{"surface":"யானே","parts":[{"text":"யான்","lemma":"யான்","gloss":"I"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"I indeed"}]}],"literal":"Because of the existence of many years along with living days / 'My life does not leave,' saying thus, lamenting much, / walking slowly with many short steps, using a staff as a leg, / with hair like spread-out thread, sleeping, / my mother of old age, who does not go out of the front yard, / and with a paled body, suffering as grief afflicts, / holding on her waist many small children, / she who has breasts withered from being squeezed to eat, greatly distressed, / plucking the tender young shoots sprouted from the plucked spots of the rubbish-heap greens, without salt, / placing them on the fire with water as the boiling pot, without buttermilk, / forgetting the taste of cooked rice, eating green leaves, / she who has dirty, worn-out garments, not blaming virtue, / my beloved wife who does not enjoy life, / both of their hearts to rejoice, like when forest dwellers / in the wide field cleared by burning the forest / sow mountain rice, and it flourishes becoming dark, / and the rain from the clouds pours down with a rustling sound on the millet that is about to yield grain, / praising your fame of giving, my gathered / kinsfolk, who suffered as hunger consumed them, to also rejoice, / even if receiving a fierce male elephant with high, raised tusks, / if you give it with hesitation, I will not accept that gift; but if you, rejoicing, / give it so that I may be pleased, even a small / kunri seed I will accept, O Kumanan of the sharp spear! / I request you to bestow grace in the proper way, O eminent lord of fame and victory, / born in a faultless noble lineage, / I who sang of you!","translation":"My aged mother, using a staff as a leg, taking short steps, with hair like spread-out thread, sleeps without leaving the front yard, lamenting, 'My life does not leave, despite the many years of living days.' My beloved wife, her body paled and suffering from grief, holds many small children on her waist; her breasts are withered from being squeezed by them to eat. Greatly distressed, she plucks the tender young shoots sprouted from the rubbish-heap greens, and without salt or buttermilk, she boils them in water, forgetting the taste of cooked rice and eating only green leaves. Wearing dirty, worn-out garments, yet not blaming virtue, she lives a life of no enjoyment. To make both their hearts rejoice, and to make my gathered kinsfolk—who suffered as hunger consumed them—rejoice, just as the rain pours down with a rustling sound from the clouds on the mountain rice and millet sown by forest dwellers in the wide fields cleared by burning, I praise your fame of giving. O Kumanan of the sharp spear! Even if I were to receive a fierce male elephant with high, raised tusks, I will not accept that gift if you give it with hesitation. But if you give it with a rejoicing heart so that I may be pleased, I will accept even a tiny kunri seed. I request you to bestow your grace in the proper way, O eminent lord of fame and victory, born of a faultless noble lineage, I who have sung of you!","modern":"வாழும் நாட்களுடன் பல ஆண்டுகள் இன்னும் இருப்பதனால், 'என் உயிர் என்னை விட்டுப் போகாது' என்று பலவாறு வருந்தி, கையில் உள்ள கோலையே காலாகக் கொண்டு, குறிய பல அடிகளை எடுத்து வைத்து மெல்ல நடந்து, நூல் விரித்தாற்போன்ற நரைமுடியை உடையவளாய், கண் துயின்று, முற்றத்தை விட்டும் வெளியே போகாத முதுமையுடைய என் தாயும்; பசலை பாய்ந்த உடம்போடு துன்பம் வருத்த வருந்தி, தன் இடுப்பில் பல சிறு குழந்தைகளைத் தாங்கி, அவர்கள் பால் குடிக்கப் பிசைந்து தின்றதால் வற்றிய முலைகளை உடையவளாய், மிகவும் மனமழிந்து, குப்பையில் முளைத்த கீரையின் கொய்த இடத்தில் மீண்டும் துளிர்த்த முற்றாத இளந்தளிர்களைக் கொய்து கொண்டு, உப்பும் இல்லாமல், மோரும் இல்லாமல், நீரையே உலையாக ஏற்றி, வெந்த சோற்றின் பதத்தை மறந்து, அந்தப் பச்சைக் கீரையையே உணவாக உண்டு, அழுக்குப்படிந்து கிழிந்த ஆடையை உடுத்தி, அறநெறியைப் பழிக்காமல் வறுமையிலும் செம்மையோடு வாழும் என் அன்பான மனைவியும்; ஆகிய இவ்விருவரின் நெஞ்சமும் மகிழவும், கானவர்கள் காட்டை எரித்துத் திருத்திய அகன்ற கொல்லை நிலத்தில் ஐவன நெல்லை விதைக்க, அது மேகம் சூழ்ந்து அழகாக வளர்ந்து, கதிர் ஈனும் பருவம் எய்திய தினைப் பயிரின் மேல் மேகம் ஒலியோடு மழையைப் பொழிந்தாற்போல, வாரி வழங்கும் உனது புகழைப் பாடித் திரண்ட, பசியால் வாடிய என் சுற்றத்தாரும் மகிழவும்; உயர்ந்த தந்தங்களை உடைய கொல்களிறைப் பரிசிலாகப் பெற்றாலும், நீ மனமில்லாமல் தரும் பரிசிலை நான் ஏற்றுக்கொள்ள மாட்டேன். நீ உவந்து மகிழ்ந்து நான் இன்புறத் தருவாயானால், மிகச் சிறிய குன்றிமணியையும் நான் ஏற்றுக்கொள்வேன், கூர்மையான வேலை உடைய குமணனே! வெற்றிப் புகழும், குற்றமற்ற உயர்ந்த குடியில் பிறந்த புகழும் உடைய, இசை சிறந்த தோன்றலே! உன்னைப் பாடிய எனக்கு முறைப்படி அருள் செய்ய வேண்டுகிறேன்.","explanation":"The poet Peruñcittiraṉār is singing to the patron Kumaṇaṉ, describing the extreme poverty of his household to evoke the patron's generosity, while maintaining his self-respect as a poet. He vividly describes his aged mother, who can barely walk and laments her long life, and his beloved wife, who feeds their children with saltless, buttermilk-less boiled greens plucked from rubbish heaps, yet never blames virtue. He compares the patron's potential generosity to the timely rain that falls on the forest fields of the mountain dwellers, bringing joy to his starving kinsfolk. The poet asserts his dignity by stating that he would reject even a majestic war elephant if given with hesitation or without respect, but would happily accept a tiny kunri seed if given with love and joy. This poem belongs to the Puram genre, specifically the theme of 'parisil kaṭānila' (demanding or requesting gifts), highlighting the noble character of both the poet and the patron.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}